Package: ubuntu-gts9u-device
Version: 2.42
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: Ubuntu gts9uwifi port contributors <noreply@example.invalid>
Depends: systemd, e2fsprogs, gdisk, parted, util-linux, cloud-guest-utils,
 gnome-shell, python3, python3-gi, python3-dbus,
 protection-domain-mapper, bluez, alsa-ucm-conf, pulseaudio-utils,
 fprintd, libpam-fprintd,
 libfprint-2-2 (>= 1:1.94.7+tod1-0ubuntu5~24.04.8+gts9u46),
 hexagonrpcd, libssc, iio-sensor-proxy,
 libcamera-gts9u (= 0.7.2+53.g62d4bfc-gts9u5),
 libspa-0.2-libcamera-gts9u (= 1.0.5-gts9u10),
 v4l2-relayd-gts9u (= 0.1.2-gts9u15)
Description: Device support for the Samsung Galaxy Tab S9 Ultra Wi-Fi
 Board-specific integration for the SM-X910 (gts9uwifi) running an Ubuntu
 userspace on a mainline kernel:
 .
  * first-boot root filesystem expansion on the microSD;
  * two-tier swap, which this image had none of: 8 GiB of zstd-compressed zram
    in front of a 16 GiB swapfile created on the internal UFS at first boot;
  * ANA38407 panel recovery after Samsung's cold-boot hand-off;
  * late audio DSP boot, which the ALSA card and the sensors both depend on;
  * the native Bluetooth address, read read-only from the Samsung EFS;
  * the UCM profile for the four CS35L45 speakers and the digital microphones;
  * the sensor recovery that hands the DSP accelerometer to the desktop, and
    the accelerometer mount matrix this panel needs;
  * automatic, hash-pinned restore of the EF-DX920 pogo keyboard application,
    without which a controller left on V34 makes the cover silent;
  * the commercial names for this SoC and GPU, so every tool that asks the
    system what it is running on gets an answer a person recognises;
  * the libwacom description without which the desktop treats the S Pen as
    an external tablet and never rotates it with the screen;
  * fprintd lifecycle integration for the secure EL721 in-display reader;
  * camera device permissions and rear-main autofocus support for libcamera's
    software ISP;
  * four automatic V4L2 camera devices for browsers and legacy apps;
  * a safe GNOME quick-settings flashlight toggle;
  * initramfs pruning for this device's 8 MiB init_boot partition.
 .
 Hardware enablement lives in the kernel and in the firmware overlay installed
 by the TWRP ZIP; this package only carries userspace integration.
